# The scaffold

This repo was made from [duckviz-scaffold]({{ scaffold_repo }}), release **{{ kit_ref }}**. The scaffold gives every
app of this kind the same architecture, commands, docs and skills, and brings new capabilities to all of them.
`copier update` changes this file: write this app's differences in docs/deviations.md.

## What comes from where

| Kind | Where | How it changes |
|---|---|---|
| **Shared code** | the `duckkit` package (a dependency in pyproject.toml, at the same release) | only in the scaffold; `copier update` moves the version |
| **Template-managed files** | the list below | `copier update` merges the scaffold's changes in, keeping this repo's edits |
| **This app's files** | everything else: `src/{{ package }}/`, the contract, the pages, the domain skills, most docs | never touched by an update |

Template-managed files:
- `CLAUDE.md` (this app's rules are in `.claude/project-rules.md`, which it imports)
- `pyproject.toml` (keep this app's dependencies; the merge keeps them)
- `.gitignore`, `.python-version`, `.streamlit/config.toml`
- `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, `.github/workflows/scaffold-update.yml`
{%- if privacy_hook %}
- `.githooks/pre-commit`
{%- endif %}
{%- if cloud_run %}
- `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, `.gcloudignore`, `docs/hosting.md`
{%- endif %}
- `docs/scaffold.md`, `docs/cli.md`
- `tests/app/test_contract_only.py`
- the skills: `app`, `app-check`, `catch-up`, `scaffold-update`{% if motherduck %}, `publish`{% endif %}{% if backup %}, `backup`{% endif %}{% if cloud_run %}, `hosting`{% endif %}

The answers this repo was made with (its name, port, and feature flags) are in `.copier-answers.yml`.

