## Updating

`/scaffold-update` (or the weekly `scaffold-update` workflow, which opens a PR) brings in a newer release:
1. `uvx copier update --trust` re-renders the template at the old and the new release with this repo's answers, and
   applies the difference here as a 3-way merge. This repo's edits stay. A clash shows as conflict markers.
2. The duckkit version in pyproject.toml moves with it; `uv lock` picks it up.
3. The tests, ruff and `uv run {{ project_name }} doctor` must pass.

The scaffold's CHANGELOG says what each release adds and any steps to take by hand.

## A new capability

When you build something here that every app of this kind could use, build it in the scaffold instead:
1. In the scaffold repo, `/upstream` takes the change: code into duckkit (with tests), files into the template
   (behind a flag if not every app wants it), and a CHANGELOG entry. The scaffold's CI renders and tests sample apps.
2. A release (a `vX.Y.Z` tag) publishes it.
3. Each app gets it with `/scaffold-update`.
